AB  - The rapid integration of artificial intelligence into many human activities has produced a growing conversation about its psychological consequences on users. The main focus of the comprehensive responses of AI users in this research is the cognitive and emotive aspects of its influence on human psychology. Using the data collected from a varied group of users, this study exposes the influence of AI interactions on user perceptions, emotions, and mental processes. Key results show that although artificial intelligence technologies can significantly boost productivity, inspire innovation, and simplify decision-making, they can also cause anxiety, reliance, and changed social behaviors. The paper investigates essential concerns, including the psychological consequences of deepfake technology, the possibility of artificial intelligence recording human rights violations, and the consequences of AI-driven monitoring. It stresses both positive and negative effects. Furthermore, under evaluation are consumers' degrees of adaptation to the growing influence of artificial intelligence and the variations in psychological reactions among different user groups. This study underlines the need for transparency, user autonomy, and ethical AI deployment by pointing out ways that AI developers and stakeholders might apply to lower unexpected psychological effects. This thorough investigation helps to clarify how artificial intelligence shapes human psychological experiences and supports a sensible approach that maximizes benefits and reduces possible risks. The research aims to guide the path of following artificial intelligence developments, thereby ensuring technologically conscious and user-centric technological innovations.
ER  - 

