AB  - Deep Neural Networks (DNN) are prominent in most applications today. From self-driving cars, sentiment analysis, surveillance systems, and robotics, they have been used extensively. Among DNNs, Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) have achieved massive success in computer vision applications as the human visual system inspires their architecture. However, striving to achieve higher accuracies, CNN complexity, parameters, and layers were increased, which led to a drastic surge in their size, making their deployment challenging. Over the years, many researchers have proposed various techniques to alleviate this issue-one of them being Design Space Exploration (DSE) to minimize size and computation with little compromise to accuracy. MobileNet V3 is one such architecture designed to achieve good accuracy while being mindful of resources. It produces an accuracy of 88.93% on CIFAR-10 with a size of 15.3MB. This paper further reduces its size to 2.3MB while boosting its accuracy to 89.13% using DSE techniques. It is then deployed into NXP's i.MX RT1060 Advanced Driver Assistance System (ADAS) platform.
ER  - 

