AB  - The increasing frequency and severity of pandemics across the globe necessitate advanced tools to predict and mitigate future outbreaks. This review paper explores the role of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in forecasting pandemics by analyzing massive, diverse datasets like health records, environmental changes, and even social media posts. AI technologies can enable early detection of a potential threat, along with identification of hot spots, facilitating prompt proactive measures to contain the threat. Machine learning algorithms are instrumental in modeling the spread of infectious diseases, enabling public health authorities to make timely interventions and strategic resource allocation. The paper also highlights the challenges of using AI, including data accuracy and privacy, as well as the ethical concerns around relying on AI for such critical decision-making. The review concludes with a discussion on the future directions of AI in pandemic preparedness, emphasizing the need for interdisciplinary collaboration to develop robust, scalable, and ethically sound AI systems that can better anticipate and respond to global health threats.
ER  - 

