AB  - With a broad range of applications for users, recommender systems (RSs), which are made to provide individualized content, have become a crucial technological answer. Despite the fact that numerous RSs have been created and successfully used in various domains, traditional AI-driven RSs continue to encounter difficulties such as data sparsity, cold start problems, and diversity maintenance. By combining artificial intelligence (AI) and human intelligence (HI), augmented intelligence (AuI) makes up for their shortcomings while maximizing their individual strengths. It has been demonstrated that combining artificial intelligence (AI) and human intelligence (HI) improves each technology's capabilities and produces better results than utilizing each technology alone. Recommender systems, which provide predictions for a variety of goods to help consumers with personalized suggestions, have grown in popularity and usefulness. These systems guarantee that they provide users with useful and efficient help by concentrating on particular item categories and utilizing strategies intended to produce tailored recommendations. Particularly during the COVID-19 lockdown, online material streaming has become the most popular kind of entertainment in recent years. Prominent streaming services use a variety of product recommendation techniques to draw customers in and make content recommendations that suit their tastes, which increases user retention. Several recommendation systems are used by well-known streaming services like Netflix, Amazon Prime, and Hulu to improve user experience. However, serious problems including the first-rater dilemma, data sparsity, and computing complexity frequently cause these systems to struggle with accuracy and consistency. In information science, security issues have emerged as a crucial subject of user discourse. E-commerce is becoming increasingly popular as a fundamental part of the Information Science framework. Ironically, though, people are growing more cautious as security and privacy risks increase. Notably, the banking sector has entered a new era as a result of e-commerce, which has changed its services and operations.
ER  - 

