AB  - The widespread adoption of autonomous driving systems (ADSs) is expected to reduce accidents caused by human error and enhance public safety. However, during the transitional period, ADS-equipped vehicles will coexist with manually driven vehicles and pedestrians, creating a mixed traffic environment. Discrepancies in communication between ADSs and other travelers may inadvertently introduce public safety risks. To address this challenge, the authors have previously proposed a high-level operational concept that promotes ethical communication among road users based on P.F. Strawson's concept of reactive attitudes. Using this concept, an ADS architecture was defined and the communication requirements for improving public safety in mixed-traffic environments were clarified. In this study, the previously proposed operational concept is further developed by systematizing the entire community as an enterprise. Using the unified architecture framework (UAF), the enterprise architecture is defined to continuously improve public safety across an entire community. The focus is particularly on promoting cooperative behavior among road users based on ethical values and forming a network to spread public safety awareness within a community. This study contributes to a sustainable and safe traffic environment through promoting ethical cooperation between ADSs and road users.
ER  - 

